      "content": "After removing the base cover and idling the dishwasher, proceed with caution if you decide that a minor tilt might suffice for draining any residual moisture. However, precautions should be taken when tilting the unit to avoid spills. Use a flashlight or headlamp if necessary to inspect the area below the base.\n\nLook closely at the drain area and the space around the sensor for signs of blockage or irregularities. If you find what seems to be a stuck or jammed sensor, try gently sliding it back and forth. Do not force it, as this may damage the unit. If you're unsure about your findings or if the sensor does not move freely, it's recommended to consult a professional to avoid any damage. Damaging an electrical component can not only cause further issues, but it may also void any remaining warranty.",
